id: pm-baksix
title: "GH-1104: health must not certify pending lossless merge receipts as reconciled"
description: "A pending merge receipt created by a lossless comment union remains state=pending while health reports ok=true. Existing pm-lwmstb correctly distinguishes lossless provenance from lossy decisions, but GitHub #1104 demonstrates that the green gate still implies reconciliation that did not occur. Publish a non-blocking-to-data but health-visible pending-receipt finding, route remediation to pm merge reconcile, and prove history-repair cannot hide it."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:merge",diagnostics,"github:1104"
created_at: "2026-08-24T15:23:02.991Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-24T21:59:35.509Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-24T21:59:34.878Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-24T21:59:34.878Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: A lossless pending merge receipt makes the health gate non-green with receipt-aware remediation; history-repair cannot clear the finding; pm merge reconcile settles it; lossy decision classification remains distinct
parent: pm-dj98
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "Pending merge receipt evidence remains health-visible until exact reconciliation settles every trusted copy; malformed, divergent, stale, aliased, or partial-settlement evidence fails closed before history mutation."
actual_result: "Health, validation, history repair, and merge reconciliation now share bounded receipt inspection and exact provenance proof. Divergent same-ID copies refuse before mutation; matching partial settlements remain pending until every copy is reconciled; lossless and lossy findings remain distinct."
